    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d850">

                <pb facs="0788" n="776" sameAs="frus:frus1944v05/pg776"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890E.01/9–1344</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of Telephone Conversation, by the Assistant
                        Chief of the Division of Near Eastern Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Kohler</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1944-09-13">September 13, 1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I called M. Baudet<anchor n="10" xml:id="d850-f1"/> today and confirmed to him
                    that a decision had been taken to extend full recognition to the Republics of
                    Syria and Lebanon, as was suggested to him by Mr. Alling<anchor n="11"
                        xml:id="d850-f2"/> in their conversation on September 7.<anchor n="12"
                        xml:id="d850-f3"/>
                </p>
                <p>M. Baudet asked whether we were seeking the approval of the French authorities. I
                    told him that it was my understanding that we were simply giving them friendly
                    advance notice on the assumption that there was no need for clearance with them
                    since they were themselves receiving an Envoy Extraordinary and Minister
                    Plenipotentiary from the Republics of Syria and Lebanon and since other Powers
                    had exchanged such representatives with these States.</p>
                <p>M. Baudet thanked me for this information and said that they would inform their
                    “Government”.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d850-f1" n="10" xml:id="d850-f1-content">
                <p>Philippe Baudet, member of the Delegation of the French Committee of National
                    Liberation in the United States.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d850-f2" n="11" xml:id="d850-f2-content">
                <p>Paul H. Alling, Deputy Director of the Office of Near Eastern and African
                    Affairs.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d850-f3" n="12" xml:id="d850-f3-content">
                <p>Memorandum of conversation not printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
